WIRE.md §4.1, §4.2: a clashing template still meets later fields (c meets b's x3); two templates of one field that expand to a common key, and a template whose keys start with `$`, are the template's fault (pairsTemplate).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Pair {
  k: Int
  v: Int
}

local record R {
  a: Int @json("x5")
  b: [Pair](..=9) @json(pairs: ["x{i}", "y{i}"])
  c: Int @json("x3")
  d: [Pair](..=20) @json(pairs: ["z{i}", "z1{i}"])
  e: [Pair](..=9) @json(pairs: ["$p{i}", "q{i}"])
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3316]  a/a.canon:10:3
  wire key x5 of b collides with a

error[E3316]  a/a.canon:11:3
  wire key x3 of c collides with b

error[E3316]  a/a.canon:12:3
  @json(pairs:) template "z1{i}" must contain {i} exactly once, differ from the other one and expand to keys that start with no $ and collide with no other key

error[E3316]  a/a.canon:13:3
  @json(pairs:) template "$p{i}" must contain {i} exactly once, differ from the other one and expand to keys that start with no $ and collide with no other key

4 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
